  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Final result\n\nDefine the two-sided normalized vector overlap by\n\n$$\n\\mathcal S_{\\rm vec}(A,B)=\n\\frac{\\langle L_A|R_B\\rangle}\n{\\langle L_A|0\\rangle\\,\\langle0|R_B\\rangle}.\n$$\n\nDefine the coefficient- and vacuum-normalized Q determinant by\n\n$$\n\\mathcal S_Q(A,B)=\n\\frac{\\displaystyle\n \\det N^{AB}/\\bigl(c_A^{\\rm ref}\\Psi_B^{\\rm ref}\\bigr)}\n{\\displaystyle\n \\left.\\det N^{AB}/\\bigl(c_A^{\\rm ref}\\Psi_B^{\\rm ref}\\bigr)\n \\right|_{A=B=\\rm vacuum}}.\n$$\n\nAll $b$'s are expressed in terms of the $a$'s as\n\n$$\nb_{21}=-\\frac{z_1(z_1-z_3)}\n {a_{12}z_2(z_2-z_3)},\\qquad\nb_{32}=-\\frac{z_2^2(z_1-z_3)}\n {a_{23}(z_1-z_2)z_3^2},\n$$\n\nwith either\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{c|c|c}\n&b_{31}&a_{12}a_{23}/a_{13}\\\\ \\hline\n{\\rm I}&-\\dfrac{z_1^2}{a_{13}z_3^2}\n&-\\dfrac{z_2(z_1-z_3)}{z_1(z_2-z_3)}\\\\[3mm]\n{\\rm II}&-\\dfrac{z_1}{a_{13}z_3}\n&-\\dfrac{z_1-z_3}{z_2-z_3}\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\nFor both branches, exactly and symbolically,\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\mathcal S_{\\rm vec}(A,B)=\\mathcal S_Q(A,B)\n\\quad\\text{for every }A,B=1,\\ldots,8.}\n$$\n\nThus all eight diagonal norms agree and all 56 cross-state scalar products vanish on both sides.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
